well today's news conference held by  planned parenthood governor steve  sisilak and other state leaders just  wrapped up this all in response to  today's historic decision by the u.s  supreme court to overturn roe v wade now  sasha loftus joins us live this  afternoon in north las vegas with more  sasha  christian yes as you mentioned that  press conference just wrapped up local  leaders state leaders here just really  voicing their opinions and voicing their  reactions after today's historic  decision we have democratic senator  jackie rosen here with us thank you so  much for joining us and you kind of  shared this during today's press  conference but what was your general  reaction to today's news well thank you  for having me but let me tell you it is  devastating news it is devastating to  women girls across this country  my daughter woke up this morning and had  less rights  than she had yesterday and less rights  than i've had for nearly 50 years of my  life so it's really important that we  find a way to codify roe v wade to be  sure that women have the right to make  their own reproductive choices to be  sure that women don't die if they show  up in emergency room with an ectopic  pregnancy or a miscarriage there's so  many things that we have to protect a  young child a victim of rape or incest  and so we really have to do everything  we can to mobilize organize expand our  democratic pro-choice majority in the  senate to protect the lives of women all  across this country and you were  speaking of the importance of people  getting out and voting on either side of  the aisle and nevada is one of nine  states where abortion is protected under  the state constitution so if you could  just kind of speak a little bit about  the importance in your opinion of  getting out to vote here at the local  level and really all around the country  i think it's important that we work at  our local state and federal level and  although we do have roe v wade we have  it codified here into law  let's be clear  if you have a mag of republican for  governor  they can do a lot of things to try to  restrict access to abortion if you don't  reelect senator catherine cortez masto  and you have someone like mega  republican adam laxalt who has  cheered on this as a big victory and  wants to impose a nationwide ban on  abortion a nationwide ban on women's  rights  then you have to mobilize organize and  get out and vote in november and beyond  it matters  thank you so much again democratic  senator jackie rosen joining us today  after today's emergency press conference  put on by planned parenthood
 

